# Terraform
.terraform/

# NOT ignored: terraform/.terraform.lock.hcl is committed deliberately.
#
# plan and apply run as separate jobs on separate runners, each doing its own
# `terraform init`. Without a committed lock file each one resolves providers
# against the registry independently, and every provider in versions.tf floats
# on a major-version constraint -- so a release landing between the two inits
# makes the saved plan un-appliable:
#
#   Error: Inconsistent dependency lock file
#   The given plan file was created with a different set of external
#   dependency selections than the current configuration.
#
# That is a race against the registry, so it fails at random. The lock file
# pins exact versions and hashes for linux_amd64 (CI) plus both darwin
# architectures. Update it deliberately:
#
#   terraform init -upgrade
#   terraform providers lock \
#     -platform=linux_amd64 -platform=darwin_arm64 -platform=darwin_amd64
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
tfplan
*.tfplan

# The upstream module is checked out at deploy time, never committed
module/

# Local overrides / secrets
*.auto.tfvars.local
.env

dev/openmetadata-infra/terraform/.terraform